// Example showcase script demonstrating all capabilities of the Rexallie visual novel engine

@set affinity_nikita = 0
@set met_nikita = false

start:
    // Setup initial background and play chill music
    @setBackground campus instant
    @playMusic chill fadeIn:1.5

    // Show Alice sliding in from the left
    @showCharacter Alice left aya_base base fadeIn:1.0 slideFrom:left

    Alice <aya_base> [base]:
    Welcome to the Rexallie VN Engine showcase!
    We've just faded in the campus background, started playing the chill soundtrack, and had me slide in from the left.

    Alice <aya_base> [happy]:
    Next, let's bring in another character. Meet Nikita!

    // Show Nikita sliding from the right
    @showCharacter Nikita right base base fadeIn:1.0 slideFrom:right
    @set met_nikita = true

    Nikita <base> [base]:
    Hello there. I hear we're showing off screen effects.

    Alice <aya_base> [base]:
    We sure are! Let's start with a camera shake to show impact.

    // Play cat sound and shake screen
    @playSFX cat
    @shake 0.8 15.0

    Nikita <base> [happy]:
    Whoa! That was a loud cat noise and a strong screen shake!

    Alice <aya_base> [happy]:
    And now, let's focus on Nikita using the camera zoom action.

    // Zoom in on Nikita
    @zoom x:300 y:0 percentage:40 time:1.5

    Nikita <casual> [happy]:
    My portrait just changed to casual, and the camera zoomed in directly on me!
    During zoom and camera movements, dialogue skipping will automatically skip these animations.

    Alice <aya_base> [base]:
    Let's reset the zoom and make a choice to show conditional branching.

    @zoom reset time:1.0

    Alice <aya_base> [base]:
    Nikita, what is your favorite topic in game dev?

    @choice
        "Ask about programming." -> path_programming
        "Ask about visual arts." -> path_art
    @endchoice

path_programming:
    @set affinity_nikita += 5
    Nikita <base> [happy]:
    Ah, coding! That's my absolute favorite. 
    It's the skeleton that holds the visual novel engine together.
    @jump evaluate_outcome

path_art:
    @set affinity_nikita -= 2
    Nikita <base> [base]:
    Art is nice, but I'm more of a logic person myself.
    @jump evaluate_outcome

evaluate_outcome:
    // Check points to determine response
    @if affinity_nikita > 0 jump high_affinity
    @if affinity_nikita <= 0 jump low_affinity

high_affinity:
    @playMusic pump fadeIn:1.0
    Nikita <casual> [happy]:
    I really enjoyed talking to you. Let's make a great visual novel together!
    @unlock_cg gallery_image_showcase
    @jump ending

low_affinity:
    Nikita <base> [base]:
    Well, thanks for chatting anyway. I have to go back to debugging now.
    @jump ending

ending:
    @hideCharacter Nikita fadeOut:0.5 slideTo:right

    Alice <aya_base> [happy]:
    That concludes our engine capabilities showcase!
    We've demonstrated:
    - Text styling tags like <b>bold</b>, <i>italics</i>, and <size=130%>size changes</size>.
    - Transitions and effects (shake, zoom, fade).
    - Conditionals, variables, branching choices, and persistent CG unlocks.

    Alice <aya_base> [base]:
    Check out the documentation in the workspace root to see how you can write your own scripts.
    Bye-bye!

    @stopMusic fadeOut:2.0
    @wait 2.0
